# KS-1185 (F4 only) — Wednesday's task for Ornith, VITEST, **TEST-ONLY MODE, ONE NEW TEST FILE**

Written 2026-09-17 from origin develop `1125607e978d6ad637720c985e43e3d79fecdf88` (#1010's squash, KS-1183). The product
file `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/routes/verification.ts` (1470 lines, blob `04b3d980f`, the #1010 gate's
equality target) was read at `:72-127`, `:409-427` and `:930-1060`. The sibling test
`ks1087-workflow-approve-deletes-the-pending-document.test.ts` (blob `4450587dc`) was read whole. The #1010 gate verdict
(F4, statement 3) and its tamper table were read. **PRE-MEASURED** in a scratch clone at the tip; see
`## Premises (measured)`. **This is a PARTIAL of KS-1185:** F1 (validate the override), F2 (idle timer) and F3 (late
error log) are NOT in this task.

## THE MODE — read this twice

TEST-ONLY, ONE NEW FILE. Your diff contains EXACTLY ONE file: the NEW test file
`Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1185-workflow-approve-forward-default-bound.test.ts`, written as
`--- /dev/null` then `+++ b/…`, one `@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@` hunk, every line `+`.
**Do NOT modify `routes/verification.ts`**, and do NOT modify `ks1087-workflow-approve-deletes-the-pending-document.test.ts`.
`verification.ts` is in files[...] only so you can see the lines the new test reaches. Do NOT copy or modify the reference
test (`notifications.test.ts`); ignore it. The checker plants the tamper named at the bottom into a clone of
`verification.ts` and expects the 🔴 cell RED and the 🟢 control GREEN, then expects both GREEN at the untouched tip.

## What is wrong (one paragraph)

KS-1183 bounded the approve route's forward to originate: `createVerificationRoutes` destructures
`originateForwardTimeoutMs = ORIGINATE_FORWARD_TIMEOUT_MS` (`:426`, the constant is `15_000` at `:127`) and arms the
forward with `proxyReq.setTimeout(originateForwardTimeoutMs, …)` (`:1030`). `index.ts` passes no override, so production
runs on that default. But every ks1087 cell passes `originateForwardTimeoutMs: 1_000`, and the only default cell reads the
exported constant as `> 0` and `< 30_000`. So the #1010 gate set the destructure default to `0` (production never times
out), and the constant to `16_000` and `29_999`: 0 of 402 cells went red. **This task:** a NEW file builds the REAL route
WITHOUT the override, spies on `http.ClientRequest.prototype.setTimeout` (calls pass through), and reads the bound the
forward request is armed with. It then runs that call's own timeout callback, so the route answers 502 now instead of
after 15 real seconds.

## Where (no product site changes — this list is informational; every line below STAYS)

- `:127` — (correct) `export const ORIGINATE_FORWARD_TIMEOUT_MS = 15_000;` — read by the new test. Stays.
- `:426` — (correct) `    originateForwardTimeoutMs = ORIGINATE_FORWARD_TIMEOUT_MS,` — the default under test. The tamper replaces this line. Stays.
- `:1030` — (correct) `          proxyReq.setTimeout(originateForwardTimeoutMs, () => {` — the call the spy reads. Stays.
- `:1031` — (correct) `            proxyReq.destroy(new Error(`originate did not answer within ${originateForwardTimeoutMs} ms`));` — the message the cells read from the error log. Stays.
- `:1041` — (correct) `          res.status(502).json({ … code: 'ORIGINATE_FORWARD_FAILED' … status: forwardStatus } });` — the 502 the cells read. Stays.

## The test — CREATE THE NEW FILE `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1185-workflow-approve-forward-default-bound.test.ts`

**Harness:** `vitest run` inside `Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway` (`package.json` scripts.test; `vitest.config.ts`,
globals, node environment). To run this file alone:
`npx vitest run src/__tests__/ks1185-workflow-approve-forward-default-bound.test.ts`.

Each cell starts a loopback originate that accepts the forward and never answers, and a real express app on loopback
with the REAL `createVerificationRoutes`, a stub Redis and a `vi.fn` log. `drive(override, fireTheBound)` installs a
pass-through spy on `http.ClientRequest.prototype.setTimeout`, POSTs approve, waits until the forward is armed and
originate holds it, records every bound the spy saw, optionally runs the spied call's own callback, and returns the
status, elapsed ms, bounds, logged `error` values, delete count and originate hits. No network beyond 127.0.0.1.

**Reproduce the body below EXACTLY as written.** It is 108 lines. Do not shorten it, do not replace any part with a
comment, do not invent a helper, do not rename a variable, do not collapse the cells into a loop or an `it.each`. Every
name a cell reads (`drive`, `PRODUCTION_DEFAULT_MS`, `OVERRIDE_MS`, `verification`) is declared or imported ABOVE the
first cell. **The file contains no backslash anywhere; keep it that way.** The template literals use `${…}` with no
backslash before the dollar sign.

```ts
// KS-1185 F4 (KS-1183 gate on #1010): no cell built the approve route WITHOUT originateForwardTimeoutMs, so the
// production default was never exercised: the default set to 0 (never), 16_000 or 29_999 reddened 0 of 402 cells.
// These cells build the REAL route and read the bound the forward request is armed with, without waiting 15 s.
import { describe, it, expect, afterEach, vi } from 'vitest';
import express from 'express';
import http from 'node:http';
import type { AddressInfo } from 'node:net';
import type { RequestHandler } from 'express';
import * as verification from '../routes/verification';

const DOC_ID = 'doc-ks1185';
const WFI_ID = 'wfi-ks1185';
/** The bound index.ts gets today, because it passes no override (ORIGINATE_FORWARD_TIMEOUT_MS, KS-1183). */
const PRODUCTION_DEFAULT_MS = 15_000;
/** A short override, so the control can let the real timer fire. */
const OVERRIDE_MS = 300;

type Log = (level: 'info' | 'warn' | 'error', message: string, meta?: object) => void;
type Drive = { status: number; ms: number; bounds: unknown[]; errors: unknown[]; deletes: number; hits: number };

const servers: http.Server[] = [];
const restores: Array<() => void> = [];

afterEach(async () => {
  for (const restore of restores.splice(0)) restore();
  for (const server of servers.splice(0)) {
    server.closeAllConnections();
    await new Promise<void>((r) => server.close(() => r()));
  }
});

async function listen(server: http.Server): Promise<number> {
  servers.push(server);
  server.listen(0, '127.0.0.1');
  await new Promise<void>((r) => server.once('listening', () => r()));
  return (server.address() as AddressInfo).port;
}

const sleep = (ms: number) => new Promise<void>((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));

async function drive(override: number | undefined, fireTheBound: boolean): Promise<Drive> {
  const pendingDocs = new Map([[DOC_ID, { title: 't', contentHash: 'h', createdBy: 'u' }]]);
  let deletes = 0;
  let hits = 0;
  const instance = { status: 'pending_approval', documentId: DOC_ID, steps: [{ name: 'Approve' }], currentStepIndex: 0 };
  const originatePort = await listen(http.createServer((req) => { hits++; req.resume(); }));
  const log = vi.fn<Log>();
  const deps = {
    authenticateToken: (): RequestHandler => (_req, _res, next) => next(),
    mockBodyParser: express.json({ limit: '1mb' }),
    query: vi.fn(async () => ({ rows: [] })) as never,
    isDbAvailable: () => false,
    redisService: {
      getWorkflowInstance: vi.fn(async (id: string) => (id === WFI_ID ? structuredClone(instance) : null)),
      setWorkflowInstance: vi.fn(async () => undefined),
      getPendingDocument: vi.fn(async (id: string) => pendingDocs.get(id) ?? null),
      deletePendingDocument: vi.fn(async (id: string) => { deletes++; pendingDocs.delete(id); }),
    } as never,
    services: { originate: { url: `http://127.0.0.1:${originatePort}` }, anchoring: { url: '' } } as never,
    log,
    memWorkflowToDocumentMap: new Map(),
    memRejectedDocuments: new Map(),
    dbSaveRejection: vi.fn(async () => undefined),
    ADMIN_ROLES: ['ADMIN'],
    enforceDocumentTypeRules: vi.fn(async () => ({ ok: true, docType: {} })) as never,
    createWorkflowInstanceIfRequired: vi.fn(async () => ({ gated: false })) as never,
    meetsVerificationLevel: () => true,
  };
  const app = express();
  app.use(verification.createVerificationRoutes(override === undefined ? deps : { ...deps, originateForwardTimeoutMs: override }));
  const gatewayPort = await listen(http.createServer(app));
  const spy = vi.spyOn(http.ClientRequest.prototype, 'setTimeout');
  restores.push(() => spy.mockRestore());
  const started = Date.now();
  const reply = fetch(`http://127.0.0.1:${gatewayPort}/api/workflow-instances/${WFI_ID}/approve`, { method: 'POST', signal: AbortSignal.timeout(3_000) })
    .then((res) => res.status, () => 0);
  // Wait until the route has armed the forward AND originate holds the request, then read the bound.
  for (let waited = 0; (spy.mock.calls.length === 0 || hits === 0) && waited < 2_000; waited += 10) await sleep(10);
  const bounds = spy.mock.calls.map((call) => call[0]);
  const onTimeout = spy.mock.calls[0]?.[1];
  if (fireTheBound && typeof onTimeout === 'function') onTimeout();
  const status = await reply;
  const errors = log.mock.calls.filter(([level]) => level === 'error').map(([, , meta]) => (meta as { error?: unknown } | undefined)?.error);
  return { status, ms: Date.now() - started, bounds, errors, deletes, hits };
}

describe('KS-1185 F4 — workflow approve built without an override arms the production default bound', () => {
  it('🔴 KS-1185 F4 — no override: the forward is armed with 15000 ms, and that bound answers 502 and keeps the document', async () => {
    const out = await drive(undefined, true);
    expect(out.bounds, 'the bound the forward request was armed with, override absent').toEqual([PRODUCTION_DEFAULT_MS]);
    expect(out.bounds).toEqual([verification.ORIGINATE_FORWARD_TIMEOUT_MS]);
    expect(out.status, `answered after ${out.ms} ms`).toBe(502);
    expect(out.errors).toEqual(['originate did not answer within 15000 ms']);
    expect(out.hits).toBe(1);
    expect(out.deletes).toBe(0);
  });

  it('🟢 KS-1185 control — with a 300 ms override the real timer fires on its own, through the same setTimeout call', async () => {
    const out = await drive(OVERRIDE_MS, false);
    expect(out.bounds).toEqual([OVERRIDE_MS]);
    expect(out.status, `answered after ${out.ms} ms`).toBe(502);
    expect(out.ms).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(OVERRIDE_MS - 50);
    expect(out.ms).toBeLessThan(OVERRIDE_MS + 1_500);
    expect(out.errors).toEqual(['originate did not answer within 300 ms']);
    expect(out.hits).toBe(1);
    expect(out.deletes).toBe(0);
  });
});
```

Why each cell is what it is:
- **🔴 KS-1185 F4** at the tip: the route built with NO override arms the forward with `[15000]`, which equals the exported
  constant. Running that call's callback answers 502, logs `originate did not answer within 15000 ms`, originate was hit
  once, and nothing is deleted. Under the tamper (`:426` default → `0`, the gate's Q-DEFAULT-0) the first `expect` fails
  **by assertion** (`expected [ +0 ] to deeply equal [ 15000 ]`). The constant set to `16_000` or `29_999`, or the
  destructure default set to `16_000`, reds the same line.
- **🟢 control**: the same harness WITH a 300 ms override, and nothing fired by hand. The spy sees `[300]`, the REAL timer
  fires on its own (502 at ~306 ms), and the log says `within 300 ms`. It proves that the spy reads the call Node really
  arms, and that the callback the 🔴 cell runs is the one the timer runs. It is green under the tamper, because an override
  never reads the default.

## Red cells

- 🔴 KS-1185 F4 — no override: the forward is armed with 15000 ms, and that bound answers 502 and keeps the document

## Tamper (test-only mode — the checker plants this in a clone to prove your cells can go red)

line: 426
from: `    originateForwardTimeoutMs = ORIGINATE_FORWARD_TIMEOUT_MS,`
to: `    originateForwardTimeoutMs = 0,`
statement_ok: the `from` line is one element of the `const { … } = deps;` destructure (`:411-427`). Its only job is the default for an absent `deps.originateForwardTimeoutMs`, and no other element or line reads or re-defaults it (4 case-insensitive occurrences in the file: `:115` the interface field, `:426` this default, `:1030-1031` the setTimeout call and its message). `to` keeps the element, so it still compiles (project tsc rc 0). The default becomes `0`, the #1010 gate's Q-DEFAULT-0 row (production never times out).

## Output

Exactly ONE ```diff block containing ONLY the new test file: `--- /dev/null` with NO leading space, then
`+++ b/Blockchain/Dev/services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1185-workflow-approve-forward-default-bound.test.ts`, then
`@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@`, then the 108 lines above, each prefixed with `+`. Blank lines are a bare `+`. No hunk for
`verification.ts` or any other file.

## Premises (measured)

All times AEST 2026-09-17, each read from `date` in the run that produced it. Scratch clone = `git clone --shared` by SHA
in a fresh `mktemp -d` under the session scratchpad (`ks1185_pm.vzK6da`), farmed and built by
`tasks/code_patch/prepare_clone.sh` (rc 0, 04:38:37–04:38:44). Scripts `scratchpad/ks1185/premeasure.sh` and
`ks1185/final.sh`, outputs `premeasure.q1.out`, `premeasure.r1.out` and `final.fin*.out`. **Every vitest, tsc and checker
run was wrapped in `sandbox-exec` with off-host outbound denied (loopback allowed).** This harness is loopback only, and
no baseline red appeared.

- **P1 tip.** origin develop = `1125607e978d6ad637720c985e43e3d79fecdf88` (`git ls-remote`, 04:36:51, 04:40:56 and 04:42:17; object local, `cat-file -t` = commit, 04:36:51). Clone HEAD equal.
- **P2 the product at the tip.** `verification.ts` blob `04b3d980f` (the #1010 gate's equality target), 1470 lines, sha256 `72ff7db4f4c017ef…`. `:127`, `:426`, `:1030` and `:1031` hold the lines quoted in `## Where`. `from` occurs once; `originateForwardTimeoutMs` occurs 4 times case-insensitively (python over the clone copy, 04:42:17).
- **P3 the gap, re-measured in scope.** ks1087 alone at the tip: 11 / 11 green (04:42:28). Under Q-DEFAULT-0 (`:426` → `= 0`, anchor count 1 → 0, project tsc rc 0): ks1087 alone **11 / 11 green** (04:42:37). The gate measured the same for the whole suite (0 / 402).
